# Inkling 2 Mini prompt pass on the M4 Pro (Metal): the MXFP8 coda's quads layout with the grouped tile holding a block's words and
# decoding by integer (gemm_routed.metal MX8Q, BLOOMERY_METAL_MX8=quads) against the rows layout (MX8R, BLOOMERY_METAL_MX8=rows), one
# binary, lever arms (round metalpp, task 1). The shipped quads tile, read a word a value a step with MX8R's float decode, was 0.68 %
# slower than rows on this prompt (m1ab2: rows 1.898..1.903 s, quads 1.913..1.920 s, 6 rounds [measured]).
# [derived] from the lab (`metal_gemm_time --ink2`, one pass of the pair + down tiles over a synthetic 128-expert coda stack, GPU
# intervals, run-to-run scatter 0.01 ms): MX8 visit-pass layer time rows 13.50 ms, old quads 14.78 ms (+9.4 %), new quads 12.99 ms
# (-3.8 % vs rows) at m = 512; m = 389: 11.35 / 12.71 / 10.95 ms. A prompt of 901 ids is passes of 512 and 389 rows over 4 MXFP8
# visits: rows 4 (13.50 + 11.35) = 99.4 ms, old quads 110.0 ms (the A/B's +13 ms is inside this +10.6 ms with its interval), new
# quads 95.8 ms: new quads - rows = -3.6 ms of 1902 ms = prompt_tok_s +0.19 %. The rest of the pass is untouched (NVFP4 tile and
# MX8R measured unmoved in the same lab: planes 11.380 / 11.381 ms, rows 13.490 / 13.492 ms before / after the shared Hold edit).
# Not under another resource's shadow: the tile is issue-bound (its DRAM time is 4.2 ms of 13 per visit-pass).
# Ruler: the lead's prompt A/B scatters 0.1 % (6 rounds); the predicted +0.19 % is inside the interval of a six-round ab, so the card
# is a non-inferiority one: the question the A/B answers is "quads is no longer slower than rows", not the size of a 0.2 % gain.
kind: noninf
question: is the Inkling 2 Mini prompt pass with the MXFP8 coda as quads (the tile holds a block's words, integer decode) not slower
  than with the coda as rows, on the M4 Pro? (before: 0.68 % slower)
term: prompt_tok_s of the prompt pass @ generate_metal -n 1 --ignore-eos --print-ids, prompt = the first 2600 bytes of the tree's
  README.md (901 ids: passes of 512 and 389 rows), Inkling-2-Mini-mlx4, M4 Pro, no --profile — (quads - rows) / rows, paired by round
unit: %
predict: 0.0..0.4
rounds: 6
sd: 0.1 % measured on m1ab2 (rows 1.898..1.903 s over 6 rounds, A/A twin within 0.4 %)
margin: 0.5 % the old quads lost 0.68 % and the decode gain it buys is 4.2 %; a quads arm within 0.5 % of rows is not a prompt
  regression worth a second layout, and the lead's A/B interval at 6 rounds is +-0.18 %
condition: one binary (target/release/generate_metal of the metalpp tree), arms quads, rows and rows2 (the A/A twin) alternate round by
  round with the order rotated each round, BLOOMERY_METAL_MX8 the only difference; each launch under both Mac model locks after
  runprof-guarded.sh's precheck (available memory >= 21 GiB, swap growth <= 2 GiB, disk >= 12 GiB); the --print-ids lists of the three
  arms equal
decide-in: quads is not slower than rows: land the tile change with the decode A/B kept (-4.2 % stays); the lab's -3.6 ms is the
  record of the small gain
decide-below: quads still slower than rows by more than the margin: the pass loss is not in the grouped tile; read the other consumers
  of the layout (arena permutation, check_weights_align, the pass's Bytes) and the e2e step against the rows arm; do not land
decide-above: quads faster than rows by more than 0.4 %: the tile's decode share is larger than the lab's MX8 visit-pass model; re-run
  the lab with the real routing (skewed) and say which term was wrong before pricing the same edit for the NVFP4 planes tile
